1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Every layer of an AI data center is an optimization problem a verifier can check.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
A Nemotron agent team on Crusoe, scored on held-out tasks it never saw.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
The team works from a Shared Brain. A Reviewer reads You.com and proposes changes.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The verifier measures every claim. A change ships only if the gain is real.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Hall layout: the DoneTwin checker re-scores every Nemotron proposal.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
The verifier rejects any layout that fails a check: here, a collision with column C1.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,500
Rack placement: 6 proposed changes, 4 kept by the gate.

8
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:42,000
On 6 unseen instances: 0.597 for v0 cold, 0.845 for the final team.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Each kept change is a paper. The gate checks its claimed gain against the measured one.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Hall: the Reviewer switched on a verifier-guided search tool. 0.688 → 0.728 on 6 unseen halls.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
All 4 layers now beat v0 cold on held-out tasks. Kernels 20% → 60% correct; inference 31% less per correct answer.

